Each cold/warm fixture fixes initial owner/generation state, complete canonical keys, proof choices and admission order, and reports lookup, comparison, authentication, construction, replay, application and simultaneous storage separately. Sufficient, immediate-insufficient and consumed-prefix twins cover new boundaries and failures; changed keys, stale references, eviction and post-flush renewed numerical inputs follow (`rule:nrz:tiles-streams-cache-charge`). This is a dependency and evidence specification, not permission to label repeated construction a cache hit.

**Decision (Family authority evidence boundary)** · `dec:nrz:lc-evaluation-family-evidence`

The closing evidence for (`claim:nrz:lc-closing-lc-family-authority`) is CAS and bindings authority for the adopted manifest plus native membership/application tested independently in both formats. Indexed-layout integration and general walk/flush execution establish their own claims as assigned in (`tab:nrz:lc-evaluation-family-evidence-allocation`). Separating the original family theorem and authenticated application from the indexed lowering that consumes them makes each claim independently reviewable without dropping integrated evidence. Family closure requires the complete evidence within this scope; it is not established by this design decision. Full LC closure still requires all allocated layout, execution and lifecycle evidence.

The family boundary requires independent expected-claim receiving-store replay; original-source, target, quantifier, face, epoch and companion mutations; weak/strong pi twins preserving complete candidates; original restoration for every admitted fibre/future tag; branch-union refusals; and literal cold/warm/cache-application evidence for each admitted schema. Native evidence proves the arithmetic and current attachment directly in binary32 and binary64, including fresh data and changed companions, without claiming indexed-layout delivery from scalar fixtures. The ten semantic fixture families remain obligations: record which use an admitted family theorem, which use the supported exact fallback, and which retain unresolved outcomes. No excluded combination becomes an unconditional answer merely to satisfy a fixture.

The dependency order remains (`rule:nrz:backlog-lc-order`): generic cache, lowerings and bounded walk precede family acceptance; later LC indexed integration and stream acceptance demonstrate their own execution evidence. Deferring general walk/flush integration evidence does not defer the generic dependency or its tests. Full LC completion still requires the combined sample/branch fixture, every supported layout in both formats, lifecycle evidence and scale evidence under (`crit:nrz:lc-evaluation-acceptance`). Separate source-substitution schema/replay, finite face/lift certificates, future-ray/gauge certificates and both-format containment checks may be implemented as partial increments; none alone discharges the closing claim.

